const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"负面词不一定是负面消息",en:"A negative word is not always bad news"},body:{zh:"Loughran与McDonald指出，通用词典中的负面词在财务文件里可能只是术语。例如负债、税或成本经常是在描述会计项目。研究问题是词典是否测到了财务语气，还是不经意测到了行业与文件写法。",en:"Loughran and McDonald question whether general-purpose negative-word lists measure financial tone. Terms for liabilities, taxes or costs may simply describe accounting items. A dictionary can inadvertently capture industry or document conventions instead of adverse information."}},{title:{zh:"样本经过多层筛选",en:"The sample is filtered"},body:{zh:"原文使用1994—2008年的EDGAR年度10-K及10-K405文件，排除修订文件，并连接CRSP与Compustat。满足标识、价格、收益、财务信息和文本长度等条件后，留下50,115个公司年度、8,341家公司。管理层讨论部分另有识别与长度筛选，不能把子样本直接当成全样本。",en:"The study uses 1994–2008 EDGAR 10-K/10-K405 filings, excluding amendments, matched to CRSP and Compustat. Identity, price, returns, accounting and document-length requirements leave 50,115 firm-years from 8,341 firms. MD&A analyses apply additional extraction and length filters."},reference:{url:"https://www.uts.edu.au/globalassets/sites/default/files/adg_cons2015_loughran-mcdonald-je-2011.pdf",label:{zh:"原文第II.A节：10-K样本",en:"Original §II.A: the 10-K sample"}}},{title:{zh:"先解析，再计数",en:"Parsing comes before counting"},body:{zh:"作者采用词袋表示，但计数前先排除表格与附件，减少模板语言的干扰。文中还比较词频比例与词项加权，避免高频词压过真正有信息的词。因而“全文分析”在这里不是把下载文件每个字符直接分词：解析范围本身就是方法的一部分。",en:"The bag-of-words pipeline excludes tables and exhibits to reduce boilerplate contamination. Proportional counts are compared with term weighting, which reduces domination by frequent words. Here, full-document analysis has a defined parsing boundary; it is not indiscriminate tokenization of every downloaded character."},reference:{url:"https://www.uts.edu.au/globalassets/sites/default/files/adg_cons2015_loughran-mcdonald-je-2011.pdf",label:{zh:"原文第II.B与II.E节：解析与加权",en:"Original §§II.B and II.E: parsing and weighting"}}},{title:{zh:"发现不是一条交易信号",en:"The finding is not a trading signal"},body:{zh:"作者发现通用词典存在显著语境误分类，财务负面词表及加权方案能改变与文件披露反应的关系。但引言也明确指出，比较的语气指标没有显示出其检验中的未来收益可预测性。能描述同期市场反应，不等于能提前获利。",en:"The authors report substantial contextual misclassification and show that financial dictionaries and term weighting change relations with filing reactions. They also report no future-return predictability from the competing tone measures in their tests. Describing an announcement response is not the same as forecasting profits."}},{title:{zh:"读方法时追踪事件窗口",en:"Track the event window"},body:{zh:"第II.D节把披露反应定义为提交日及随后三日的持有期超额收益，并说明基准与控制变量。建议把文本范围、词表版本、分母和事件时间一起记录：即使词典相同，换成新闻标题、中文公告或另一种事件窗口，也不是同一项测量。",en:"Section II.D defines a filing-date response over days 0–3 and specifies the benchmark and controls. Track text boundaries, dictionary version, denominator and event timing together. The same dictionary applied to headlines, Chinese announcements or another window defines a different measurement."}},{title:{zh:"中文材料需要另行验证",en:"Chinese documents need separate validation"},body:{zh:"编辑建议：中文文本的分词、否定、歧义与财务术语要在人工标注样本上验证，不能逐词翻译英语词典后宣称等效。保留文件哈希与修订关系，才能区分语气变化、解析器变化和重复转载；不要把数据清理差异解释成公司行为变化。",en:"Editorial application: validate Chinese segmentation, negation and domain terms against labeled material; translating an English dictionary does not establish equivalence. Preserve document hashes and revisions to distinguish tone changes from parser changes or syndicated copies."}}],readerLimits:{zh:"词典是有版本、有语境的测量工具，不是对事实真伪或投资价值的自动判断。",en:"A dictionary is a versioned, context-dependent measurement tool, not an automatic judgment of truth or investment value."}};export{e as default};
